===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|id=vital liquid|inh|enm>blood>vital liquid|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|blood}}, from {{inh|en|ang|blōd}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*blōd}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*blōþą}}, possibly from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*bʰel-||}} ("to swell") + -ó- (thematic vowel) + -to (nominalizer), i.e. "that which bursts out". Cognate with {{cog|stq|Bloud}}, {{cog|fy|bloed}}, {{cog|nl|bloed}}, {{cog|de|Blut}}, {{cog|da|-}}, {{cog|sv|-}} and {{cog|no|blod}}, {{cog|is|-}} and {{cog|fo|blóð}}.

